{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/148053-p-tc-vs-d-td-who-wins-in-an-interrogation","id":148053,"title":"P:tC VS D:tD - Who wins in an interrogation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-24T12:52:07-07:00","id":148053,"title":"P:tC VS D:tD - Who wins in an interrogation?","content":"Hey there again,<br /> <br /> In our current game we are pitted against some demons and angels, and I wanted to know just HOW MUCH is a demon a perfect liar?<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> Promethean uses Confession on a demon and succeeds. Can he speak normally?<br /> Promethean uses Hearing the inner voice, can he lie about his thoughts?<br /> Promethean uses In Vino Veritas, does the demon simply becomes drunk but does not care about interogation?<br /> Promethean uses Remove Inhibition, is the demon still in control?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T17:36:32-07:00","id":148281,"title":"","content":"Here's how I'd probably rule these situations:<br /> <br /> <b>Confession:</b> the demon blurts out whatever he's thinking at the time, as normal. However, the demon adds his Cover, not Primum, to contest the roll unless in demonic form, and so probably has lots of dice.<br /> <b>Hearing the Inner Voice:</b> the Promethean hears the demon's thoughts, as normal. Again, the demon adds Cover, not Primum, to contest.<br /> <b>In Vino Veritas:</b> the demon suffers light-headedness and forgets the interrogation afterwards as normal, and is compelled to answer, but not compelled to be truthful. Again, contest with Cover.<br /> <b>Remove Inhibitions:</b> the demon loses all inhibitions and reacts accordingly, as normal.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, here are the relevant properties of the Unchained as they may relate to the situation. These represent the large bulk of the Unchained's reputation as invisible liars, and if you're not falling into any of these pitfalls, it still works on them.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernatural Resistance:</b> Demons in human form use Cover, not Primum, as their Supernatural Tolerance. They can choose to use Primum instead, but this results in a visible electric, staticky aura, and threatens their Cover.<br /> <b>Spoof:</b> Demons in human form targeted by an effect that reveals a target to be supernatural (Aura Sight, for example) can roll Cover reflexively and, on success, have the effect react as if the demon were a mortal human.<br /> <b>Total Control:</b> Demons have perfect control over their facial expressions, body language, microexpressions, any other outward sign of what they're inwardly thinking.<br /> <b>Liar's Tongue:</b> Thoughts formed in the demon's mind assume an aspect of truth or falsehood as the demon chooses. No supernatural power can reliably read whether something the demon has thought or said is true or false, only what the demon wishes the power to read it as. Outward evidence may disprove the demon's claims regardless; for example, if the demon says the sky is neon orange, and you look outside and the sky is cloudy blue, a power to identify whether the demon is being honest will say the demon is honest, but you still know the sky isn't orange, man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 05-24-2014, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T17:45:26-07:00","id":148286,"title":"","content":"I'd venture the Demon may be able to Spoof <b>Hearing the Inner Voice</b> as it may very well blow his cover. Otherwise I'd say Loserman's assessments seem accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T21:11:47-07:00","id":148368,"title":"","content":"What Master Loserman said.<br /> <br /> To add nuance, I'd say that &quot;Hearing the Inner Voice&quot; would reveal the &quot;Cover's&quot; inner thoughts if the Demon resists, adding a level of confusion for the Promethean (mostly, to preserve what Demon's are good at, and also, it seems like a neat idea).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T09:53:49-07:00","id":150448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/148053-p-tc-vs-d-td-who-wins-in-an-interrogation?p=148368#post148368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Master Loserman said.<br /> <br /> To add nuance, I'd say that &quot;Hearing the Inner Voice&quot; would reveal the &quot;Cover's&quot; inner thoughts if the Demon resists, adding a level of confusion for the Promethean (mostly, to preserve what Demon's are good at, and also, it seems like a neat idea).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with this since Demon's exist in a state of Quantum fluctuation with the Cover and the Demon is the Cover but can sometimes choose not to be the cover. The Demon chooses what the cover thinks and the cover blurts it out along with everything else the cover may be thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}